From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:59:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: apple: sleep: add apple,ps-keep-on

Some power state words that one machine's macOS raises to on for the
commit are left alone by another machine's macOS on the same SoC. Let
the device tree name the words the sleep driver must not raise.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml   | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
index bdbe2a5cca..be0f2a31a2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
@@ -55,6 +55,13 @@ properties:
       Pins of that controller to leave alone across a sleep, neither saved nor
       put back.
 
+  apple,ps-keep-on:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    description:
+      Power state words, as offsets into the PMGR power state block, that the
+      SoC's sleep would raise for the commit but that this machine's macOS
+      leaves as they are. They are neither raised nor put back.
+
   apple,debug-port:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description:
-- 
2.43.0

